\author{utensil}
\date{2026-08-12}

\p{A finite group becomes linear once its elements are used as a basis. This
route starts with that construction, passes through modules, semisimple
blocks, and characters, and then follows normal subgroups, computation, and
twisted multiplication. The explicit quaternion calculations earlier in
these notes are test cases for this general route, not substitutes for it.}

